/*!
@defgroup etmr_pwm_driver eTMR PWM Driver (eTMR_PWM)
@ingroup etmr
@details
@brief PWM mode driver for the eTMR peripheral.

## Overview

The PWM sub-module supports independent and complementary PWM generation
with configurable duty cycle, period, alignment mode, dead-time insertion,
fault protection, and software/hardware trigger synchronization.

## Features

- Independent and complementary channel modes
- Edge-aligned, center-aligned, and asymmetrical alignment
- Duty cycle specified in percentage or raw ticks
- Dead-time insertion for complementary pairs
- Fault input protection with per-channel safe-state values
- Software trigger for synchronized register updates
- Phase offset for asymmetrical PWM

## Usage Pattern

@code{.c}
#define ETMR_INST (0U)

etmr_state_t state;
etmr_user_config_t config;

/* Step 1: Initialize common driver */
eTMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&config);
eTMR_DRV_Init(ETMR_INST, &config, &state);

/* Step 2: Configure and start PWM */
etmr_pwm_param_t pwmParam = { ... };  /* Fill in channel configs */
eTMR_DRV_InitPwm(ETMR_INST, &pwmParam);

/* Step 3: Update duty cycle at runtime */
eTMR_DRV_UpdatePwmChannel(ETMR_INST, 0U, 5000U, 0U,
                           eTMR_PWM_UPDATE_IN_DUTY_CYCLE, true);

/* Step 4: Issue software trigger to apply updates */
eTMR_DRV_SyncWithSoftTrigger(ETMR_INST);

/* Step 5: De-initialize */
eTMR_DRV_DeinitPwm(ETMR_INST);
eTMR_DRV_Deinit(ETMR_INST);
@endcode

## API Quick Reference

### Initialization
| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_InitPwm() | Initialize counter, period, channels, and faults. |
| eTMR_DRV_DeinitPwm() | Stop all PWM channels and reset configuration. |
| eTMR_DRV_InitPwmChannel() | Initialize individual PWM channel output modes. |
| eTMR_DRV_InitPwmDutyCycleChannel() | Initialize duty cycles for configured channels. |

### Update
| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_UpdatePwmChannel() | Update duty cycle and phase offset for one channel. |
| eTMR_DRV_UpdatePwmPeriod() | Update PWM period (frequency or ticks). |
| eTMR_DRV_UpdatePwmPeriodAndDuty() | Update period and duty cycle simultaneously. |

### Fault
| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_InitFault() | Configure fault protection settings. |

### Trigger
| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_SyncWithSoftTrigger() | Issue software trigger for sync. |

*/
